/*
 * Fast ASCII-path check functions for common string methods.
 * Each returns: 1 = True, 0 = False, -1 = need Python fallback (non-ASCII chars)
 * These operate directly on the raw array buffer, avoiding Python object
 * creation and method call overhead.
 *
 * For Unicode arrays, strings are null-*padded* (not null-*terminated*).
 * The effective string length is determined by the LAST non-null character.
 * Characters after the last non-null are padding and ignored.
 * Embedded nulls (before the last non-null) are real characters.
 */

